;; A variant inside a table whose declared maximum is one: the group is present
;; in a record or it is absent from it, and where it is present its one entry
;; chooses its own alternative.
;;
;; The pair is with odo-optional and with variant-sliding at once. odo-optional
;; varies a table's presence and holds no alternation; variant-sliding holds one
;; and varies a table's length. This entry is the intersection, and it is the
;; shape a consumer reaches only after it agrees that a maximum of one is a
;; table: until then the REDEFINES inside the group is a REDEFINES outside every
;; table, which is two descriptions of the whole record rather than one
;; alternation chosen per occurrence. A reader built that way does not read this
;; file wrongly -- it has no arm to take at all.

;; The encoding profile. All four axes, always, with no default for any.
;; ASCII rather than EBCDIC because the whole of this entry's claim is which
;; bytes a record does and does not contain, and a reviewer checking a
;; hand-computed byte string should be able to read it in a hex dump.
(encoding
  (charset ascii)
  (sign-convention ascii-zone-37)
  (byte-order big-endian)
  (float-format ieee-754))

;; VB, and not a free choice: the reading below makes the record's extent move
;; with its own count, and a variable-extent record type is refused on a
;; fixed-length dataset. The four records of this file are 5, 12, 12 and 5
;; bytes.
(framing
  (recfm VB))

(record DETAIL
  (copybook "detail.cpy" VOP-DETAIL))

;; `odoslide`, which is what makes the group's absence move VOP-TAIL and what
;; makes the alternation inside it a variant. Under `noodoslide` the same
;; copybook describes a different file *and* a different descriptor: the group
;; always present, every record a fixed 12 bytes, and the REDEFINES two record
;; types rather than two arms. Nothing in the bytes disagrees with the wrong
;; reading, which is why this form is required rather than inferred.
(copybook-reading
  (occurs-depending-on odoslide))

;; Nothing selects the record type: every record in this file is a detail.
(discriminate DETAIL single-record-type)

;; The alternation, and what tells the two alternatives apart: a kind byte that
;; sits inside the entry the choice is being made for.
(discriminate-variant (item DETAIL VOP-NOTE VOP-NOTE-BODY)
  (arm VOP-NOTE-BODY (equals (item DETAIL VOP-NOTE VOP-KIND) "T"))
  (arm VOP-NOTE-CODE (equals (item DETAIL VOP-NOTE VOP-KIND) "C")))

(sequence (* DETAIL))
